  abstract = {We address the problem of automatically recognizing
artistic movement in digitized paintings. We make the fol-
lowing contributions: Firstly, we introduce a large digitized
painting database that contains refined annotations of artis-
tic movement. Secondly, we propose a new system for the
automatic categorization that resorts to image descriptions
by color structure and novel topographical features as well
as to an adapted boosted ensemble of support vector ma-
chines. The system manages to isolate initially misclassi-
